THIRD-PARTY LICENCES FOR LAWH
=============================

This file lists the licences of the third-party code and data built into the lawh binary that
came with it. lawh itself is under the MIT licence: see LICENSE, next to this file.

It has three parts:

1. Fonts. The binary embeds two fonts under the SIL Open Font License 1.1: Inter (licence in
   Inter-OFL.txt) and Libertinus Math (licence in Libertinus-OFL.txt), both next to this file.

2. Rust crates, below, grouped by licence. Generated by cargo-about for this build target from
   lawh's Cargo.lock. Where a crate offers a choice of licences, the one shown is the one lawh
   uses it under. Each crate is listed with its version, repository and authors. A few crates
   ship no licence file; for those the licence's standard text is shown, and its copyright
   holders are the crate's authors listed with it, or, where a crate lists none, the
   contributors of its repository.

3. Embedded notices, at the end: NOTICE files and the licences of data compiled into the binary
   (Typst's own notices, CSL styles, syntax definitions, hyphenation patterns) that Rust licence
   tools don't report. They come from assets/licenses/EMBEDDED-NOTICES.txt in lawh's source.

